IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-derivative-claims.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 11, "Derivative claims and proceedings by members": Chapter 1 (derivative claims in England and Wales or Northern
-- Ireland, ss 260 to 264) and Chapter 2 (derivative proceedings in Scotland, ss 265 to 269): lines 3377-3566 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- The court's judgments (that the evidence discloses no prima facie case, that a person acting in accordance with s 172 would not seek to continue the claim, that an act could be
-- ratified) are inputs: what the court is satisfied of is the fact the text makes decisive, and the member's seat asks what follows from it. The member's own answers (s 112) are inputs.
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).

§ `Part 11, Chapter 1: derivative claims in England and Wales or Northern Ireland (ss 260 to 264)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 260 Derivative claims
-- ======================================================================================================================
-- src:3393 | (c) references to a member of a company include a person who is not a member but to whom shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law.
@ref s 260(5)(c) a transferee counts as a member (src:3393-3393)
GIVEN `s 112 the person is a member of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(5)(c) the person is a member for this Chapter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 112 the person is a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted to the person by operation of law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a member of a company include a person who is not a member but to whom shares in the company have been transferred or transmitted by operation of law"

-- src:3391 | (a) “director” includes a former director;
@ref s 260(5)(a) a former director (src:3391-3391)
GIVEN `the person is a former director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(5)(a) the person is a director for this Chapter` MEANS
    IF `the person is a former director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“director” includes a former director"

-- src:3392 | (b) a shadow director is treated as a director; and
@ref s 260(5)(b) a shadow director (src:3392-3392)
GIVEN `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(5)(b) the shadow director is treated as a director` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 251 the person is a shadow director`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a shadow director is treated as a director"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a shadow director is s 251's answer

-- src:3380 | (1) This Chapter applies to proceedings in England and Wales or Northern Ireland by a member of a company—
-- src:3381 | (a) in respect of a cause of action vested in the company, and
-- src:3382 | (b) seeking relief on behalf of the company.
-- src:3383 | This is referred to in this Chapter as a “derivative claim”.
@ref s 260(1) derivative claim (src:3380-3383)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in England and Wales or Northern Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 260(5)(c) the claimant is a member for this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of a cause of action vested in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings seek relief on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(1) the proceedings are a derivative claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the proceedings are in England and Wales or Northern Ireland`) OR (NOT `the proceedings are in respect of a cause of action vested in the company`) OR (NOT `the proceedings seek relief on behalf of the company`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Chapter applies to proceedings in England and Wales or Northern Ireland by a member of a company— (a) in respect of a cause of action vested in the company, and (b) seeking relief on behalf of the company. This is referred to in this Chapter as a “derivative claim”"
        IF `s 260(5)(c) the claimant is a member for this Chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 260(5)(c) the claimant is a member for this Chapter` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "proceedings ... by a member of a company"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the claimant is a member is s 112's answer and is not known

-- src:3384 | (2) A derivative claim may only be brought—
-- src:3385 | (a) under this Chapter, or
-- src:3386 | (b) in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (proceedings for protection of members against unfair prejudice).
@ref s 260(2) how a derivative claim may be brought (src:3384-3386)
GIVEN `it is brought under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is brought in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (proceedings for protection of members against unfair prejudice)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(2) the derivative claim may be brought` MEANS
    IF `it is brought under this Chapter` OR `it is brought in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994 (proceedings for protection of members against unfair prejudice)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A derivative claim may only be brought— (a) under this Chapter, or (b) in pursuance of an order of the court in proceedings under section 994"

-- src:3387 | (3) A derivative claim under this Chapter may be brought only in respect of a cause of action arising from an actual or proposed act or omission involving negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by a director of the company.
-- src:3388 | The cause of action may be against the director or another person (or both).
@ref s 260(3) the cause of action (src:3387-3388)
GIVEN `the cause of action arises from an actual or proposed act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(3) a derivative claim under this Chapter may be brought in respect of the cause of action` MEANS
    IF `the cause of action arises from an actual or proposed act or omission` AND `the act or omission involves negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust` AND `by a director of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A derivative claim under this Chapter may be brought only in respect of a cause of action arising from an actual or proposed act or omission involving negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust by a director of the company"

DECLARE `s 260(3) defendant` IS ONE OF
    `s 260(3) the director`
    `s 260(3) another person`
    `s 260(3) both the director and another person`

-- src:3388 | The cause of action may be against the director or another person (or both).
@ref s 260(3) against whom (src:3388-3388)
GIVEN defendant IS A `s 260(3) defendant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 260(3) the cause of action may be against the defendant` MEANS
    CONSIDER defendant
    WHEN `s 260(3) the director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 260(3) another person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 260(3) both the director and another person` THEN JUST TRUE -- "The cause of action may be against the director or another person (or both)"

-- src:3389 | (4) It is immaterial whether the cause of action arose before or after the person seeking to bring or continue the derivative claim became a member of the company.
@ref s 260(4) when the cause of action arose (src:3389-3389)
`s 260(4) it matters whether the cause of action arose before or after the person became a member of the company` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial whether the cause of action arose before or after the person seeking to bring or continue the derivative claim became a member of the company"

