-- src:3395 | (1) A member of a company who brings a derivative claim under this Chapter must apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue it.
@ref s 261(1) the member must apply for permission (src:3395-3395)
GIVEN `a member of a company brings a derivative claim under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(1) the member must apply to the court for permission to continue the claim` MEANS
    IF `a member of a company brings a derivative claim under this Chapter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member of a company who brings a derivative claim under this Chapter must apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue it"

DECLARE `s 261 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 261(1) apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the derivative claim`

-- The duty as a rule. The text states no time and no consequence of not applying: none is invented (no WITHIN; the reason on the breach says so).

-- src:3395 | (1) A member of a company who brings a derivative claim under this Chapter must apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue it.
@ref s 261(1) the member's duty to apply (src:3395-3395)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 261 action`
`s 261(1) the member's duty to apply for permission to continue the claim` MEANS
    PARTY Member
    MUST `s 261(1) apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the derivative claim`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Member BECAUSE "s 261(1): the member did not apply for permission to continue the derivative claim (the text states no consequence)"

