-- src:3410 | (2) A member of the company may apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim as a derivative claim on the ground that—
-- src:3411 | (a) the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court,
-- src:3412 | (b) the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently, and
-- src:3413 | (c) it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim.
@ref s 262(2) the member's application and its grounds (src:3410-3413)
GIVEN `s 262(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(2) the member may apply to the court for permission to continue the claim as a derivative claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 262(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the cause of action could be pursued as a derivative claim turns on s 260
        IF `s 262(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
        IF `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` AND `the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` AND `it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that— (a) the manner in which the company commenced or continued the claim amounts to an abuse of the process of the court, (b) the company has failed to prosecute the claim diligently, and (c) it is appropriate for the member to continue the claim as a derivative claim"

