-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 263 Whether permission to be given
-- ======================================================================================================================
DECLARE `s 263 when the act or omission occurs` IS ONE OF
    `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`
    `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`

-- src:3425 | (1) The following provisions have effect where a member of a company applies for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262.
@ref s 263(1) when the section applies (src:3425-3425)
GIVEN `a member of a company applies for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263(1) the provisions of this section have effect` MEANS
    IF `a member of a company applies for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The following provisions have effect where a member of a company applies for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) under section 261 or 262"

-- src:3426 | (2) Permission (or leave) must be refused if the court is satisfied—
-- src:3427 | (a) that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to continue the claim, or
-- src:3428 | (b) where the cause of action arises from an act or omission that is yet to occur, that the act or omission has been authorised by the company, or
-- src:3429 | (c) where the cause of action arises from an act or omission that has already occurred, that the act or omission—
-- src:3430 | (i) was authorised by the company before it occurred, or
-- src:3431 | (ii) has been ratified by the company since it occurred.
@ref s 263(2) permission must be refused (src:3426-3431)
GIVEN when IS A `s 263 when the act or omission occurs`
      `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to continue the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` MEANS
    IF    `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to continue the claim`
       OR (when EQUALS `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur` AND `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)`)
       OR (when EQUALS `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` AND (`the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` OR `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Permission (or leave) must be refused if the court is satisfied— (a) that a person acting in accordance with section 172 ... would not seek to continue the claim, or (b) ... authorised ..., or (c) ... authorised ... before it occurred, or ... ratified ... since it occurred" (this subsection requires no refusal on these facts)

-- src:3432 | (3) In considering whether to give permission (or leave) the court must take into account, in particular—
-- src:3433 | (a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to continue the claim;
-- src:3434 | (b) the importance that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would attach to continuing it;
-- src:3435 | (c) where the cause of action results from an act or omission that is yet to occur, whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be—
-- src:3436 | (i) authorised by the company before it occurs, or
-- src:3437 | (ii) ratified by the company after it occurs;
-- src:3438 | (d) where the cause of action arises from an act or omission that has already occurred, whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, ratified by the company;
-- src:3439 | (e) whether the company has decided not to pursue the claim;
-- src:3440 | (f) whether the act or omission in respect of which the claim is brought gives rise to a cause of action that the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company.
@ref s 263(3) the matters to be taken into account (src:3432-3440)
GIVEN when IS A `s 263 when the act or omission occurs`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF when EQUALS `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`
        THEN LIST
            "(a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to continue the claim",
            "(b) the importance that a person acting in accordance with section 172 would attach to continuing it",
            "(c) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, authorised by the company before it occurs, or ratified by the company after it occurs",
            "(e) whether the company has decided not to pursue the claim",
            "(f) whether the act or omission gives rise to a cause of action that the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company"
        OTHERWISE LIST
            "(a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to continue the claim",
            "(b) the importance that a person acting in accordance with section 172 would attach to continuing it",
            "(d) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, ratified by the company",
            "(e) whether the company has decided not to pursue the claim",
            "(f) whether the act or omission gives rise to a cause of action that the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company"

-- src:3441 | (4) In considering whether to give permission (or leave) the court shall have particular regard to any evidence before it as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter.
@ref s 263(4) members with no personal interest (src:3441-3441)
GIVEN `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263(4) the court must have particular regard to the evidence` MEANS
    IF `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any evidence before it as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter"

-- (5) to (7): the Secretary of State's power to amend (2) and (3) by regulations, the duty to consult, and the affirmative resolution procedure: machinery (inert, reason 2).

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 264 Application for permission to continue derivative claim brought by another member
-- ======================================================================================================================
-- src:3448 | (1) This section applies where a member of a company (“the claimant”)—
-- src:3449 | (a) has brought a derivative claim,
-- src:3450 | (b) has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company, or
-- src:3451 | (c) has continued a derivative claim under this section.
@ref s 264(1) when the section applies (src:3448-3451)
GIVEN `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a member of the company (“the claimant”) has brought a derivative claim` OR `the claimant has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company` OR `the claimant has continued a derivative claim under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a member of a company (“the claimant”)— (a) has brought a derivative claim, (b) has continued as a derivative claim a claim brought by the company, or (c) has continued a derivative claim under this section"

-- src:3452 | (2) Another member of the company (“the applicant”) may apply to the court for permission (in Northern Ireland, leave) to continue the claim on the ground that—
-- src:3453 | (a) the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court,
-- src:3454 | (b) the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently, and
-- src:3455 | (c) it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim.
@ref s 264(2) another member's application and its grounds (src:3452-3455)
GIVEN `s 264(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(2) another member may apply to the court for permission to continue the claim` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 264(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 264(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
        IF `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` AND `the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently` AND `it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that— (a) the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court, (b) the claimant has failed to prosecute the claim diligently, and (c) it is appropriate for the applicant to continue the claim as a derivative claim"

-- src:3456 | (3) If it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave), the court—
-- src:3457 | (a) must dismiss the application, and
-- src:3458 | (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate.
@ref s 264(3)(a) prima facie case (src:3456-3458)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave), the court— (a) must dismiss the application, and (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate"

-- src:3456 | (3) If it appears to the court that the application and the evidence filed by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for giving permission (or leave), the court—
-- src:3457 | (a) must dismiss the application, and
-- src:3458 | (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate.
@ref s 264(3)(b) consequential order (src:3456-3458)
GIVEN `s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(3)(b) the court may make any consequential order it considers appropriate` MEANS
    IF `s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court— (a) must dismiss the application, and (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate"

-- src:3459 | (4) If the application is not dismissed under subsection (3), the court—
-- src:3460 | (a) may give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company, and
-- src:3461 | (b) may adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained.
@ref s 264(4) directions and adjournment (src:3459-3461)
GIVEN `s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264(4) the court may give directions as to the evidence and may adjourn the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 264(3) the court must dismiss the application`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the application is not dismissed under subsection (3), the court— (a) may give directions as to the evidence to be provided by the company, and (b) may adjourn the proceedings to enable the evidence to be obtained" (the application is dismissed)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the application is dismissed under subsection (3) is not known

DECLARE `s 264(5) course` IS ONE OF
    `s 264(5)(a) give permission (or leave) to continue the claim on such terms as it thinks fit`
    `s 264(5)(b) refuse permission (or leave) and dismiss the application`
    `s 264(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and give such directions as it thinks fit`
    `s 264(5) some other course`

