-- src:3468 | (1) In Scotland, a member of a company may raise proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3) in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf.
@ref s 265(1) a member may raise proceedings in Scotland (src:3468-3468)
GIVEN `the proceedings are raised in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 265(7)(e) the person is a member for this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 265(3) the act or omission is one specified in subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 265(1) the member may raise the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are raised in Scotland`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In Scotland, a member of a company may raise proceedings"
        IF NOT `it is in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in order to protect the interests of the company and obtain a remedy on its behalf"
        IF `s 265(7)(e) the person is a member for this Chapter` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 265(3) the act or omission is one specified in subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 265(7)(e) the person is a member for this Chapter` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 265(3) the act or omission is one specified in subsection (3)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a member is s 112's answer, or the act is not known
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a member of a company may raise proceedings in respect of an act or omission specified in subsection (3)"

