-- src:3503 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:3504 | (a) a company has raised proceedings, and
-- src:3505 | (b) the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings.
@ref s 267(1) when the section applies (src:3503-3505)
GIVEN `a company has raised proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a company has raised proceedings` AND `the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where— (a) a company has raised proceedings, and (b) the proceedings are in respect of an act or omission which could be the basis for derivative proceedings"

-- src:3506 | (2) A member of the company may apply to the court to be substituted for the company in the proceedings, and for the proceedings to continue in consequence as derivative proceedings, on the ground that—
-- src:3507 | (a) the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court,
-- src:3508 | (b) the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently, and
-- src:3509 | (c) it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings.
@ref s 267(2) the member's application to be substituted (src:3506-3509)
GIVEN `s 267(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(2) the member may apply to the court to be substituted for the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 267(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 267(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
        IF `the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` AND `the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently` AND `it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that— (a) the manner in which the company commenced or continued the proceedings amounts to an abuse of the process of the court, (b) the company has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently, and (c) it is appropriate for the member to be substituted for the company in the proceedings"

-- src:3510 | (3) If it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it, the court—
-- src:3511 | (a) must refuse the application, and
-- src:3512 | (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate.
@ref s 267(3)(a) prima facie case (src:3510-3512)
GIVEN `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(3) the court must refuse the application` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the court that the application and the evidence produced by the applicant in support of it do not disclose a prima facie case for granting it, the court— (a) must refuse the application, and (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate"

