GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(3)(b) the court may make any consequential order it considers appropriate` MEANS
    IF `s 267(3) the court must refuse the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court— (a) must refuse the application, and (b) may make any consequential order it considers appropriate"

-- src:3513 | (4) If the application is not refused under subsection (3)—
-- src:3514 | (a) the applicant must serve the application on the company,
-- src:3515 | (b) the court—
-- src:3516 | (i) may make an order requiring evidence to be produced by the company, and
-- src:3517 | (ii) may adjourn the proceedings on the application to enable the evidence to be obtained, and
-- src:3518 | (c) the company is entitled to take part in the further proceedings on the application.
@ref s 267(4)(a) (src:3513-3518)
GIVEN `s 267(3) the court must refuse the application` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(4)(a) the applicant must serve the application on the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 267(3) the court must refuse the application`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the application is not refused under subsection (3) ... (a) the applicant must serve the application on the company" (the application is refused)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the application is refused under subsection (3) is not known

