DECLARE `s 267(5) course` IS ONE OF
    `s 267(5)(a) grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit`
    `s 267(5)(b) refuse the application`
    `s 267(5)(c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit`
    `s 267(5) some other course`

-- src:3519 | (5) On hearing the application, the court may—
-- src:3520 | (a) grant the application on such terms as it thinks fit,
-- src:3521 | (b) refuse the application, or
-- src:3522 | (c) adjourn the proceedings on the application and make such order as to further procedure as it thinks fit.
@ref s 267(5) on hearing the application (src:3519-3522)
GIVEN course IS A `s 267(5) course`
      `the court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267(5) the court's course on hearing the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is hearing the application`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On hearing the application, the court may—"
        IF course EQUALS `s 267(5) some other course`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the court may— (a) ..., (b) ..., or (c) ..." (no "only")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 268 Granting of leave
-- ======================================================================================================================
DECLARE `s 268 when the act or omission occurs` IS ONE OF
    `s 268(1)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`
    `s 268(1)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`

-- src:3524 | (1) The court must refuse leave to raise derivative proceedings or an application under section 267 if satisfied—
-- src:3525 | (a) that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to raise or continue the proceedings (as the case may be), or
-- src:3526 | (b) where the cause of action is an act or omission that is yet to occur, that the act or omission has been authorised by the company, or
-- src:3527 | (c) where the cause of action is an act or omission that has already occurred, that the act or omission—
-- src:3528 | (i) was authorised by the company before it occurred, or
-- src:3529 | (ii) has been ratified by the company since it occurred.
@ref s 268(1) leave must be refused (src:3524-3529)
GIVEN when IS A `s 268 when the act or omission occurs`
      `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to raise or continue the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(1) leave to raise derivative proceedings or an application under section 267 must be refused` MEANS
    IF    `the court is satisfied that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would not seek to raise or continue the proceedings`
       OR (when EQUALS `s 268(1)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur` AND `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been authorised by the company (before it occurs, where it is yet to occur)`)
       OR (when EQUALS `s 268(1)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` AND (`the court is satisfied that the act or omission was authorised by the company before it occurred` OR `the court is satisfied that the act or omission has been ratified by the company since it occurred`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court must refuse leave to raise derivative proceedings or an application under section 267 if satisfied— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." (this subsection requires no refusal on these facts)

-- src:3530 | (2) In considering whether to grant leave to raise derivative proceedings or an application under section 267, the court must take into account, in particular—
-- src:3531 | (a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to raise or continue the proceedings (as the case may be),
-- src:3532 | (b) the importance that a person acting in accordance with section 172 (duty to promote the success of the company) would attach to raising or continuing them (as the case may be),
-- src:3533 | (c) where the cause of action is an act or omission that is yet to occur, whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be—
-- src:3534 | (i) authorised by the company before it occurs, or
-- src:3535 | (ii) ratified by the company after it occurs,
-- src:3536 | (d) where the cause of action is an act or omission that has already occurred, whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, ratified by the company,
-- src:3537 | (e) whether the company has decided not to raise proceedings in respect of the same cause of action or to persist in the proceedings (as the case may be),
-- src:3538 | (f) whether the cause of action is one which the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company.
@ref s 268(2) the matters to be taken into account (src:3530-3538)
GIVEN when IS A `s 268 when the act or omission occurs`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 268(2) the matters the court must take into account in particular` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF when EQUALS `s 268(1)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`
        THEN LIST
            "(a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to raise or continue the proceedings",
            "(b) the importance that a person acting in accordance with section 172 would attach to raising or continuing them",
            "(c) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, authorised by the company before it occurs, or ratified by the company after it occurs",
            "(e) whether the company has decided not to raise proceedings in respect of the same cause of action or to persist in the proceedings",
            "(f) whether the cause of action is one which the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company"
        OTHERWISE LIST
            "(a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to raise or continue the proceedings",
            "(b) the importance that a person acting in accordance with section 172 would attach to raising or continuing them",
            "(d) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, ratified by the company",
            "(e) whether the company has decided not to raise proceedings in respect of the same cause of action or to persist in the proceedings",
            "(f) whether the cause of action is one which the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company"

-- src:3539 | (3) In considering whether to grant leave to raise derivative proceedings or an application under section 267, the court shall have particular regard to any evidence before it as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter.
@ref s 268(3) members with no personal interest (src:3539-3539)
GIVEN `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 268(3) the court must have particular regard to the evidence` MEANS
    IF `there is evidence before the court as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any evidence before it as to the views of members of the company who have no personal interest, direct or indirect, in the matter"

-- (4) to (6): the Secretary of State's power to amend (1) and (2) by regulations, the duty to consult, and the affirmative resolution procedure: machinery (inert, reason 2).

