-- s 269 Application by member to be substituted for member pursuing derivative proceedings
-- ======================================================================================================================
-- src:3546 | (1) This section applies where a member of a company (“the claimant”)—
-- src:3547 | (a) has raised derivative proceedings,
-- src:3548 | (b) has continued as derivative proceedings raised by the company, or
-- src:3549 | (c) has continued derivative proceedings under this section.
@ref s 269(1) when the section applies (src:3546-3549)
GIVEN `a member of a company (“the claimant”) has raised derivative proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has continued as derivative proceedings proceedings raised by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has continued derivative proceedings under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a member of a company (“the claimant”) has raised derivative proceedings` OR `the claimant has continued as derivative proceedings proceedings raised by the company` OR `the claimant has continued derivative proceedings under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a member of a company (“the claimant”)— (a) has raised derivative proceedings, (b) has continued as derivative proceedings raised by the company, or (c) has continued derivative proceedings under this section"

-- src:3550 | (2) Another member of the company (“the applicant”) may apply to the court to be substituted for the claimant in the action on the ground that—
-- src:3551 | (a) the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court,
-- src:3552 | (b) the claimant has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently, and
-- src:3553 | (c) it is appropriate for the applicant to be substituted for the claimant in the proceedings.
@ref s 269(2) another member's application to be substituted (src:3550-3553)
GIVEN `s 269(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate for the applicant to be substituted for the claimant in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 269(2) another member may apply to the court to be substituted for the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 269(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 269(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
        IF `the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court` AND `the claimant has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently` AND `it is appropriate for the applicant to be substituted for the claimant in the proceedings`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that— (a) the manner in which the proceedings have been commenced or continued by the claimant amounts to an abuse of the process of the court, (b) the claimant has failed to prosecute the proceedings diligently, and (c) it is appropriate for the applicant to be substituted for the claimant in the proceedings"

